| second countable (`ETT.tex:255`) | ⚠ weakened: not used by `massive_line`; carried by the assemblies only |
| `sing_α(M)` « a connected 1-dimensional submanifold », `M` « a differential manifold » (`prop:GX_sing_dec`, l.1435–1437) | ⚠ weakened: not assumed; the translation atlas, built from the charts into `E_κ` (`prop_isom_local`), plays its role |
| « parametrisable by `ℝ` », « inextensible », « chronal » | ✓ carried: `γ : ℝ → M` onto the component, `C.Inextensible ⊤ univ γ`, chronal over every segment, a closed embedding when `C` is causal (the field's reading) |
| `E₀` (l.1330), `Isom(E^{1,2})` (l.1333) | ✓ carried, in a reading: `Causal.E0` (OQ-34, OQ-35; it enters through the cover's family and the type invariance `E₀ ↔ E_κ`), `Flat.isom 2` (OQ-82; through `prop_isom_local`) |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

* **Why unmarked.** OQ-82 (the group), OQ-18 (« its causality »), OQ-34/OQ-35 (`E₀` in the
  family). `defi:causal_Ealpha`'s other sentences belong to other files: the model facts to
  `Causal.Model.Massive`, the `(G,X)` sentence to `Causal.Remarks.EModelsBPrime`. Whether its
  l.1341 is also a statement at `M` is a question (REPORT). `lem:past_BTZ` (a) at `α = 0` (the
  field `line`) and its (b) are not here.
* **Periodic components.** The field asks a closed embedding only when `C` is causal. A compact
  component would be the image of a periodic `γ` (`LineDevelopment.circle_line`). No witness
  with a compact massive component is built.
* **No mixed witness.** `E_π` has massive points only; the library has no manifold with points of
  both kinds (SFALocal SCOPE).

